{
  "description": "Normative seat-slot CAS vectors (scheme v2: leadership_term separated from the claimant's execution incarnation; sparse monotonic terms): every conforming seat registry (the Rust SeatSlot::fold, the cloud implementation) must reproduce these decisions and slot transitions bit-for-bit. The fold is structural only — signatures and authority are peer-side and deliberately absent here. Byte fields are fill-byte tags: `run`/`claimant`/`module` N means the 32-byte array [N; 32]. `expect.kind` matches the decision variant only (structural reasons are diagnostics, not contract). `expect_slot` is the observable projection after the step: `leased_term`/`leased_incarnation`/`leased_claimant` are null when unclaimed; `last_leadership_term` is the tombstone floor. Ordinals are pinned to <= i64::MAX (9223372036854775807) — the shared bounded domain.",
  "lease_defaults": {
    "domain": "daemon-vhc/seat-lease/2.0.0",
    "run": 1,
    "role": "coordinator",
    "epoch": 0,
    "module": 204,
    "endpoint_ws": "wss://registry.example/runs/demo/ws",
    "issued_at_ms": 1000,
    "expires_at_ms": 31000,
    "heartbeat_interval_ms": 10000
  },
  "vectors": [
